{"_comment": "Non-resident enrolment by institution (IPEDS Fall Enrolment, 2023) with SEVP's top campuses by STEM OPT authorisation beside it. F-1 ISSUANCE BY UNIVERSITY IS NOT PUBLISHED: State reports visas by consulate and nationality, never by school, and SEVP publishes school-level figures only for OPT. So this answers who ENROLS foreign students, not who receives F-1 visas, and the two are not the same question. THE THREE MEASURES COUNT DIFFERENT POPULATIONS -- IPEDS counts everyone enrolled in a fall term at every level and field, SEVP counts graduates already working on STEM OPT, and the GSS ranking elsewhere covers science, engineering and health graduate students only -- so they rank institutions differently and are reported side by side rather than blended. NON-RESIDENT IS A VISA CATEGORY: permanent residents are counted under their race and appear as domestic, so every share here is a floor. Ranked by COUNT rather than share, because share rankings at this level are dominated by very small institutions.", "sources": {"enrolment": "NCES IPEDS Fall Enrolment 2023", "stem_opt": "DHS SEVP, 2024 top 100 school campuses with STEM OPT"}, "enrolment_year": 2023, "institutions": 5898, "national": {"graduate": {"total": 3274462, "non_resident": 561020, "share": 17.1, "institutions": 2045}, "undergraduate": {"total": 16427350, "non_resident": 460000, "share": 2.8, "institutions": 5633}, "all": {"total": 19701812, "non_resident": 1021020, "share": 5.2, "institutions": 5898}}, "largest_by_non_resident_total": [{"institution": "New York University", "state": "NY", "control": "private", "non_resident": 19373, "total": 57335, "share": 33.8, "graduate_non_resident": 11549}, {"institution": "Columbia University in the City of New York", "state": "NY", "control": "private", "non_resident": 13898, "total": 35279, "share": 39.4, "graduate_non_resident": 12142}, {"institution": "University of Southern California", "state": "CA", "control": "private", "non_resident": 12754, "to